        "tool_name": "Bash",
        "input": {
          "command": "cat > /Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-7-report.md << 'EOF'\n# Task 7 Report: QueryCatalog (Named-Query YAML Loader)\n\n## Overview\nImplemented `QueryCatalog` class that loads YAML-based named queries from `config/queries/*.yaml`, compiles them to SQLAlchemy `text()` clauses, and provides a lookup interface keyed by `(file_key, name)` tuples.\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Files Created/Modified\n- **Created:** `src/server/storage/queries.py` — QueryCatalog implementation\n- **Created:** `tests/server/storage/test_queries.py` — TDD test suite\n- **Existing:** `config/queries/.gitkeep` — already present, no action needed\n\n### QueryCatalog Design\n\n**Module:** `src/server/storage/queries.py`\n\nThe class provides:\n- **`__init__(queries)`**: Internal constructor storing compiled queries in a dict keyed by `(file_key, name)` tuples\n- **`QueryCatalog.load(queries_dir)`**: Class method that:\n  - Scans `queries_dir/*.yaml` files (sorted by filename for determinism)\n  - Parses each YAML file with `yaml.safe_load()`\n  - Compiles each statement to `sqlalchemy.text()` clauses\n  - Validates that each statement is a non-empty string\n  - Detects duplicate `(file_key, name)` keys and raises `QueryConfigError`\n  - Handles YAML parsing errors and wraps them as `QueryConfigError`\n- **`get(file_key, name)`**: Returns compiled TextClause or raises `KeyError` with a \"did you mean\" listing of available queries\n\n**Error Handling:**\n- `QueryConfigError` raised for malformed YAML, empty statements, non-string values, and duplicate keys\n- `KeyError` raised on cache miss with human-readable listing of available queries (format: `file_key:name`)\n\n**Dependencies:** PyYAML, SQLAlchemy 2.0, existing `server.storage.errors.QueryConfigError`\n\n## TDD Workflow\n\n### Step 1: RED Phase (Tests Fail)\n\n**Command:**\n```bash\npython -m pytest tests/server/storage/test_queries.py -v\n```\n\n**Output (before implementation):**\n```\nERROR collecting tests/server/storage/test_queries.py _____________\nImportError while importing test module\n...\nE   ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'server.storage.queries'\n```\n\nStatus: FAIL (expected) ✓\n\n### Step 2: GREEN Phase (Tests Pass)\n\n**Command (after implementation):**\n```bash\npython -m pytest tests/server/storage/test_queries.py -v\n```\n\n**Output:**\n```\n============================= test session starts ==============================\ncollected 4 items\n\ntests/server/storage/test_queries.py::test_load_and_get PASSED           [ 25%]\ntests/server/storage/test_queries.py::test_missing_query_raises_with_listing PASSED [ 50%]\ntests/server/storage/test_queries.py::test_empty_statement_rejected PASSED [ 75%]\ntests/server/storage/test_queries.py::test_duplicate_rejected PASSED     [100%]\n\n============================== 4 passed in 0.02s ===============================\n```\n\nStatus: PASS ✓\n\n### Step 3: Commit\n\n**Command:**\n```bash\ngit add src/server/storage/queries.py tests/server/storage/test_queries.py\ngit commit -m \"feat(storage): QueryCatalog named-query loader\"\n```\n\n**Result:**\n```\n[feature/storage-layer ce18f05] feat(storage): QueryCatalog named-query loader\n 2 files changed, 71 insertions(+)\n create mode 100644 src/server/storage/queries.py\n create mode 100644 tests/server/storage/test_queries.py\n```\n\nCommit SHA: `ce18f05`\n\n## Test Coverage\n\nThe test suite validates:\n\n1. **`test_load_and_get`**: Roundtrip load→compile→get works correctly\n   - Creates a simple `ingest.yaml` with a query\n   - Loads catalog and retrieves the compiled statement\n   - Verifies the SQL text is present in the compiled clause\n\n2. **`test_missing_query_raises_with_listing`**: KeyError on cache miss includes suggestions\n   - Loads a catalog with one query `ingest:a`\n   - Attempts to get a non-existent query `ingest:nope`\n   - Verifies KeyError message contains the available query key\n\n3. **`test_empty_statement_rejected`**: Whitespace-only statements are rejected\n   - Attempts to load YAML with a statement that is only whitespace\n   - Verifies QueryConfigError is raised during load\n\n4. **`test_duplicate_rejected`**: Per-key deduplication (allows duplicates across files)\n   - Creates two YAML files (`a.yaml`, `b.yaml`) with the same query name `q`\n   - Loads successfully (no error) because `(a, q)` ≠ `(b, q)`\n   - This validates that deduplication is per-tuple, not global by name\n\n## Self-Review\n\n**Correctness:**\n- ✓ Implements exact interface from brief: `load()` classmethod, `get()` instance method\n- ✓ Proper key composition as `(file_key, name)` tuples\n- ✓ SQLAlchemy integration: uses `text()` for compilation\n- ✓ Error propagation: `QueryConfigError` for config issues, `KeyError` for lookups\n- ✓ All test cases pass\n\n**Edge Cases Handled:**\n- ✓ YAML parse errors wrapped as `QueryConfigError`\n- ✓ Non-string statement values rejected\n- ✓ Whitespace-only statements treated as empty and rejected\n- ✓ Empty YAML files parsed as empty dict (no error)\n- ✓ Per-file sorting ensures deterministic behavior\n\n**Code Quality:**\n- ✓ Type hints on public methods (`str | Path`, `dict[tuple[str, str], TextClause]`, `TextClause`)\n- ✓ Docstring follows module convention (storage.md §4 reference)\n- ✓ Single responsibility: QueryCatalog only handles loading and lookup\n- ✓ No unneeded dependencies or utilities\n\n**Testing:**\n- ✓ All assertions match brief examples\n- ✓ Uses pytest standard fixtures (`tmp_path`)\n- ✓ Covers success path, error paths, and edge cases\n- ✓ Execution time minimal (0.02s)\n\n## Concerns\n\n**None identified.** The implementation:\n- Follows the brief specification exactly\n- Uses established dependencies (PyYAML, SQLAlchemy)\n- Has no external side effects\n- Passes all validation tests\n- Fits the existing error hierarchy\n\n## Files Changed Summary\n\n| File | Type | Lines | Purpose |\n|------|------|-------|---------|\n| `src/server/storage/queries.py` | New | 38 | QueryCatalog implementation |\n| `tests/server/storage/test_queries.py` | New | 33 | Full test coverage (4 tests) |\n| `config/queries/.gitkeep` | Existing | 0 | Already present, no changes |\n\n**Total additions:** 71 lines of code + tests\nEOF\n"
